── TYPE WITHOUT A SHAPE GIVEN TO A FUNCTION THAT REFLECTS ── E0350_type_without_a_shape_given_to_a_function_that_reflects.lt:18:18  [E0350]

`fn() -> i64` has no shape: it is the field `run` of `Job`, and `leaves`
reflects on the parts of its `T`:

  18 │   print("{leaves(job)}")
     │                  ^^^

A function that reflects reads the shape of each type it reaches, and function
types, handlers and native types such as `Shared` have none. Leave such fields
out, or give the type an impl of a trait the function checks first.
